  {
    "title": "Claude Code Edits Your Repo, Not a Chat Box",
    "topic_source": "seed",
    "pillar": "coding-environments",
    "hook": "Claude Code does not answer. It acts.",
    "takeaway": "The model got tools. That is the whole jump.",
    "caption": "Claude Code does not answer. It acts.\nA chat assistant returns text you paste. An agentic coding tool reads your files, runs commands, sees the output and tries again.\n1. Prompt — you describe the change, not the diff.\n2. Read — the tool pulls the real files into context.\n3. Edit — it writes a patch to disk, not a code block.\n4. Verify — it runs your tests and reads the failure.\n5. Loop — the error becomes the next prompt, automatically.\nThat loop is why agentic tools fix bugs a chat window only describes.\n📌 Save this before your next 'paste the code back' session.\n🔁 Send it to someone still copy-pasting from a chat tab.\nWritten by Kai.\nFollow @byteflowlabs for AI systems, no hype.",
    "hashtags": [
      "#claudecode",
      "#aiagents",
      "#aiengineering",
      "#developers"
    ],
    "footage_queries": [
