    "title": "Gemini vs Claude vs GPT: Pick by Failure Mode",
    "topic_source": "seed",
    "pillar": "model-comparison",
    "hook": "Benchmarks agree. Your workload will not.",
    "takeaway": "Route by how each one fails, not by leaderboards.",
    "caption": "Benchmarks agree. Your workload will not.\nA practical way to choose between Gemini, Claude and GPT:\n1. Shape the task — long document, agentic tool use, or bulk cheap calls?\n2. Long context — huge inputs favor the model with the biggest usable window, not the biggest advertised one.\n3. Tool use — multi-step agent work rewards models that follow schemas and stop when done.\n4. Volume — high-traffic, low-stakes calls belong on the cheapest tier that passes your eval.\n5. Eval — run your own 20 real examples; that beats any leaderboard.\nOne model for everything is a billing decision, not an engineering one.\n📌 Save this before your next model migration.\n🔁 Send it to whoever picks the default model.\nWritten by Kai.\nFollow @byteflowlabs for AI systems, no hype.",
